{
    "file": "The_Strategic_and_Breakthrough_Selling.docx",
    "title": "The Strategic and Breakthrough Selling",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Strategic selling requires sales professionals to move beyond product presentation and transactional persuasion toward a deeper understanding of customer priorities, decision dynamics, competitive alternatives, value creation, and long-term commercial opportunity. Breakthrough selling adds the ability to challenge conventional approaches, uncover hidden needs, create differentiated value, and advance opportunities that may otherwise remain stalled or commoditized.",
        "This three-day course equips sales professionals and managers with practical methods for selecting and prioritizing opportunities, researching accounts, identifying decision makers and influencers, diagnosing customer needs, developing compelling value propositions, managing competitive positioning, handling objections, negotiating value, and creating disciplined opportunity strategies.",
        "Through account cases, questioning practice, stakeholder mapping, value-proposition exercises, objection simulations, negotiation scenarios, and opportunity planning, participants develop a more strategic and commercially focused approach to winning complex sales opportunities."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Sales managers, business-development managers, key account managers, account executives, senior sales professionals, relationship managers, solution-sales professionals, commercial managers, and employees responsible for developing, managing, or winning significant customer opportunities."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "The course uses an applied methodology combining short presentations, sales cases, account and opportunity analysis, stakeholder mapping, questioning and listening exercises, value-proposition development, competitive-positioning activities, objection-handling simulations, negotiation practice, role plays, peer feedback, and strategic opportunity planning."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Strategic selling",
        "Opportunity qualification",
        "Account analysis",
        "Customer-needs diagnosis",
        "Consultative questioning",
        "Stakeholder mapping",
        "Value proposition development",
        "Competitive positioning",
        "Objection handling",
        "Value-based negotiation",
        "Sales opportunity management",
        "Relationship development"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Differentiate strategic selling from transactional selling.",
        "Prioritize sales opportunities according to value, fit, probability, and strategic importance.",
        "Research customer organizations and identify relevant business priorities.",
        "Map decision makers, influencers, users, sponsors, and potential blockers.",
        "Use structured questioning to uncover explicit and underlying customer needs.",
        "Develop differentiated value propositions linked to customer outcomes.",
        "Position solutions effectively against competitors and alternative courses of action.",
        "Create momentum in complex or stalled opportunities.",
        "Handle objections without relying prematurely on discounting.",
        "Negotiate around value while protecting commercial interests.",
        "Develop clear opportunity strategies, actions, and next steps.",
        "Build stronger long-term customer relationships while pursuing profitable growth."
    ],
